/* STAGE B: THE COARSE HIT COUNTERS MOVED TO DDR, deliberately and by name.
   The stage-B code (the line-time derivation and the locked-exposure AEC) pushed the
   image past the 128 KB OCM region with 800 bytes free -- and the linker refused, it
   did not silently overflow ("section .bss will not fit in region ocm").  Rather
   than shave anything load-bearing, ONE array moved: `g_dhit`, the 80x45 byte
   consecutive-hit array (3,600 bytes, read and written once per comparison in the
   persistence pass), now lives in the free hole between FINE_SUM (ends
   0x126D7080) and BG_BASE (0x12700000).  It is CPU-only: no DMA touches it and no
   other master sees it, so ordinary cacheable DDR is the honest place for it,
   exactly as FINE_HIT/FINE_SUM (stage 8) and the readiness grids (stage 3) already
   are.  NOTHING ELSE changed address or size; DHIT[] is the same array, same index
   arithmetic, same code. */
#define DHIT         (g_cur->v_dhit)                /* PER VIEW: the coarse pass's hit counters */
/* (the declaration moved into view_state_t, see VIEW_STATE_BASE) */
/* (the declaration moved into view_state_t, see VIEW_STATE_BASE) */
